        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): wrap live-probe JSON.parse calls in try/catch",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nWrap two JSON.parse sites in live-probe helpers in try/catch: MCP loopback JSON-RPC response and cron probe argsJson. Both now produce descriptive errors instead of raw SyntaxError crashes.\n\n## Real behavior proof (required for external PRs)\n\n**Behavior addressed**: Two JSON.parse calls on potentially malformed input without error handling.\n\n**Real environment tested**: Linux, Node 22, OpenClaw branch `fix/live-probe-helpers-json-parse`\n\n**Proof command** (malformed MCP loopback response):\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/live-probe-json-parse.mts\n```\n\n**Proof script output** (scripts/proof/live-probe-json-parse.mts):\n```\n=== Proof: live-probe helpers JSON.parse hardening ===\n\nLoopback endpoint: http://127.0.0.1:42217/mcp\nResponse body: not valid json {\n\nCaught expected error: mcp loopback returned malformed JSON\n\nPASS: malformed loopback JSON produces contextual error.\n```\n\nThe proof starts a real local HTTP server on `127.0.0.1`, registers it as the active MCP loopback runtime, and calls `verifyCliCronMcpLoopbackPreflight`. The helper rejects with `mcp loopback returned malformed JSON` instead of a raw `SyntaxError`.\n\n**Regression test**:\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live-probe-helpers.test.ts\n```\n\n```\n Test Files  3 passed (3)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n```\n\nNew test \"wraps malformed loopback JSON-RPC responses with a contextual error\" verifies the malformed response path raises `mcp loopback returned malformed JSON`.\n\n**What was not tested**: Live cron probe argsJson corruption in the field (the value is generated internally with `JSON.stringify`, so the helper is defensive hardening).\n\n## Risk\n\nLow. Diagnostic/probe code, not hot-path. Errors rethrown with context.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
